1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,354
of money.

2
00:00:00,394 --> 00:00:03,434
And then came the thing that changed everything: 2008.

3
00:00:03,474 --> 00:00:07,234
Big American banks had bet people's money on home loans...

4
00:00:07,283 --> 00:00:08,048
and lost.

5
00:00:08,088 --> 00:00:09,617
A bank called Lehman Brothers,

6
00:00:09,657 --> 00:00:11,558
more than a hundred and fifty years old,

7
00:00:11,598 --> 00:00:13,287
went under in a single day.

8
00:00:13,327 --> 00:00:16,551
The American government set aside seven hundred billion dollars

9
00:00:16,591 --> 00:00:17,683
to rescue the banks.

10
00:00:17,723 --> 00:00:18,614
With whose money?

11
00:00:18,654 --> 00:00:19,698
The same people's.

12
00:00:19,738 --> 00:00:21,672
Millions lost their homes and jobs.

13
00:00:21,712 --> 00:00:22,772
And the rescued banks?

14
00:00:22,812 --> 00:00:25,201
Nine of them paid over thirty billion dollars in

15
00:00:25,241 --> 00:00:26,784
bonuses that same year.

16
00:00:26,824 --> 00:00:28,284
So the ledger keeper gambled,

17
00:00:28,324 --> 00:00:29,306
and the customer paid.

18
00:00:29,346 --> 00:00:30,295
Heads, the bank wins.

19
00:00:30,335 --> 00:00:31,763
Tails, you pay. Brilliant, sir.

20
00:00:31,803 --> 00:00:32,957
I recommend we adopt it.

21
00:00:33,093 --> 00:00:36,211
And out of that crisis came money without banks.

22
00:00:36,376 --> 00:00:38,588
The whole story is on the Earth Report channel.

23
00:00:38,829 --> 00:00:40,864
Subscribe to the channel and turn on the bell

24
